{"parentUuid":"23035cf3-23ed-4771-a473-417564acfdd5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"dcf34cb7-ee8f-4169-a004-0d53a085ee95","agentId":"ae376dabbfd7a5096","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011SKvg8iyFTE3B9y9AwUVDk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Codato Fischetti 2006 \"Combinatorial Benders' Cuts\" Operations Research experimental results LP gap\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/inm/oropre/v54y2006i4p756-766.html\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming on JSTOR\",\"url\":\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/25147009\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Combinatorial-Benders'-Cuts-for-Mixed-Integer-Codato-Fischetti/7ba61b0c68ee3b4557d888146f0f109593d96470\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/abs/10.1287/opre.1060.0286\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220244181_Combinatorial_Benders'_Cuts_for_Mixed-Integer_Linear_Programming\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Combinatorial Benders’ Cuts\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221316776_Combinatorial_Benders'_Cuts\"},{\"title\":\"On generating maximal nondominated Benders cuts | Annals of Operations Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10479-011-0883-6\"},{\"title\":\"A Benders’ decomposition algorithm with combinatorial cuts for the multi-manned assembly line balancing problem\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/ejores/v278y2019i3p796-808.html\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for the Strip Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/inm/oropre/v62y2014i3p643-661.html\"},{\"title\":\"An accelerated Benders decomposition algorithm for integrated seaside operations planning with berthing preemption | Operational Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12351-025-00940-2\"}]\n\nI found information about the Codato & Fischetti 2006 paper on Combinatorial Benders' Cuts. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Publication Details\nGianni Codato and Matteo Fischetti's \"Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming\" was published in Operations Research, Vol. 54, No. 4 (Jul. - Aug., 2006), pp. 756-766.\n\n## Methodology\nThe paper proposes an automatic problem reformulation aimed at removing the model dependency on the big-M coefficients, defining a master integer linear problem (ILP) with no continuous variables that contains combinatorial information on the feasible integer variable combinations. Master solutions are sent to a slave linear program (LP), which validates them and possibly returns combinatorial inequalities to be added to the current master ILP, with these inequalities associated to minimal (or irreducible) infeasible subsystems of a certain linear system.\n\n## LP Gap Improvements\nThis produces an LP relaxation of the master problem which can be considerably tighter than the one associated with the original MIP formulation. For MILP problems with large M's, the presence of M undermines the quality of the linear relaxation of the MILP model.\n\n## Experimental Results\nComputational results on two specific classes of hard-to-solve MIPs indicate that the new method produces a reformulation which can be solved some orders of magnitude faster than the original MIP model.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"595716f6-bcf3-4287-a532-27d623572a00","timestamp":"2026-05-09T17:49:14.973Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"23035cf3-23ed-4771-a473-417564acfdd5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"371b8bfe-1f01-42d4-af97-3f640f1d11b6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"dcf34cb7-ee8f-4169-a004-0d53a085ee95","agentId":"ae376dabbfd7a5096","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CraDNFPVfHXLfoGnSN2TDx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT nogood clause learning minimal infeasible subset CDCL\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Best way to find infeasible constraints · Issue #973 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/973\"},{\"title\":\"Conflict-driven clause learning (CDCL) SAT solvers — CS-E3220: Propositional satisfiability and SAT solvers documentation\",\"url\":\"https://users.aalto.fi/~tjunttil/2020-DP-AUT/notes-sat/cdcl.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about your query on OR-Tools CP-SAT, nogood clause learning, minimal infeasible subsets, and CDCL:\n\n## Core Architecture\n\nThe foundation of CP-SAT is a CDCL (Conflict-Driven Clause Learning) SAT solver that works with Boolean variables and clauses, extended to handle integer variables and complex constraints through lazy clause generation.\n\n## Clause Learning in CP-SAT\n\nThe key technique that makes SAT solving efficient is conflict-driven clause learning (CDCL). When the solver hits a dead end (a conflict where no valid assignment exists), it analyzes why the conflict occurred and learns a new clause preventing similar conflicts. The analysis produces a learned clause like \"NOT x OR NOT y\" meaning \"x and y cannot both be true.\" This clause is added to the problem permanently (for the duration of the solve).\n\n## Minimal Infeasible Subsets\n\nIf the model proves infeasible, CP-SAT can return a minimal subset of the assumptions, and thus the corresponding constraints, that lead to the conflict. CP-SAT offers the extraction of unsatisfiable cores from infeasible models, a capability particularly useful for model debugging. By enabling constraints conditionally using only_enforce_if(b) and adding b as an assumption, one can isolate sources of infeasibility.\n\nThe search results show that CP-SAT integrates these advanced SAT solving techniques to create an effective hybrid constraint programming solver, though the specific implementation details of nogood clause learning mechanics aren't extensively covered in the available documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fdfcef94-9641-4e37-9e1a-c9e8315e2cca","timestamp":"2026-05-09T17:49:15.667Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"371b8bfe-1f01-42d4-af97-3f640f1d11b6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
